}^{3}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want to know when the velocity is $509\\,\\text{m/s}$, we substitute $v(t)=509$ into the equation above and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}509 & =8{t}^{3}-3 \\\\ 512 & =8{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & =\\frac{512}{8} \\\\ {t}^{3} & =64 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle is $509\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=4\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264115 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264116 13194139533893 true] [17592186264115 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533893 true] [17592186264115 1041 "field-1" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264115 1104 #edb/ref 17592186264116 13194139533893 true] [17592186264115 1110 #uuid "68d81add-6401-51a8-8b81-5b150b5d0b4c" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264116 1034 "4" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264116 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533893 true] [17592186264116 1111 #uuid "d3d3f607-046a-5af8-be50-0a6370ebbbce" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264117 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264118 13194139533893 true] [17592186264117 1089 "q-316062" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264117 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533893 true] [17592186264117 1100 "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in centimeters) at time $t$ minutes is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{t}^{6}-2{t}^{4}-8{t}^{2}-7t,\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=1\\,\\text{min}.$\n\nThe speed of the particle is \n{{field-1}}$\\text{cm/min}.$" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264117 1113 #uuid "cadef097-386b-5352-9bf6-68f695d9a1ba" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264117 1145 "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{6}-2{t}^{4}-8{t}^{2}-7t) \\\\  & =18{t}^{5}-8{t}^{3}-16t-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=1,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =18(1)^{5}-8(1)^{3}-16(1)-7 \\\\  & =18-8-16-7 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-13|