\\cdot \\frac{1}{3{(\\sqrt[3]{t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t-\\frac{8}{{(\\sqrt[3]{t})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=8,$ we substitute $t=8$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(8) & =2(8)-\\frac{8}{{(\\sqrt[3]{8})}^{2}} \\\\  & =16-2 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264131 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264132 13194139533893 true] [17592186264131 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533893 true] [17592186264131 1041 "field-1" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264131 1104 #edb/ref 17592186264132 13194139533893 true] [17592186264131 1110 #uuid "0eba9b1a-d770-56ed-bbfb-7ba9e61b7fce" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264132 1034 "14" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533893 true] [17592186264132 1111 #uuid "94bd6fda-9ce8-5416-a112-bf610ec7c40e" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264133 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264134 13194139533893 true] [17592186264133 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264137 13194139533893 true] [17592186264133 1089 "q-336164" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264133 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533893 true] [17592186264133 1100 "The displacement $s$ (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by the equation $s(t)={3}^{3t+1}$, where $t$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the position ${s}_{0}$ and velocity ${v}_{0}$ of the particle at the initial moment of time $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n${s}_{0}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\text{m}\\,\\text{and}\\,$\n\n${v}_{0}=$\n{{field-2}}$\\text{m/s}$" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264133 1113 #uuid "7080eac4-3fa8-5049-bbb4-7c6a19b7e3b2" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264133 1145 "To calculate the initial position, we substitute $t=0$ it into the equation $s(t)={3}^{3t+1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{0} & =s(0) \\\\  & ={3}^{3(0)+1} \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t