{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\  & =2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}|=\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}≈2.47\\,\\text{m/s}$ to 2 decimal places." 13194139533893 true] [17592186264147 1000 #edb/ref 17592186264148 13194139533893 true] [17592186264147 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533893 true] [17592186264147 1041 "field-1" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264147 1104 #edb/ref 17592186264148 13194139533893 true] [17592186264147 1110 #uuid "1d1b1fc7-103b-534f-b174-c938159c03b0" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264148 1034 "2.47" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533893 true] [17592186264148 1111 #uuid "13f7a0b1-57c1-504c-b552-46cd17455ea8" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264149 1017 #edb/ref 17592186264150 13194139533893 true] [17592186264149 1089 "q-48904" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264149 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533893 true] [17592186264149 1100 "The displacement $s$ (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ of a particle moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis is given by the equation $s(t)=(2t+1)^{3}$, where $t$ is the time, measured in seconds. Find the position and velocity of the particle at the initial moment of time $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264149 1113 #uuid "3ae77e72-b12e-5e34-a452-174b8e1e2c84" 13194139533893 true] [17592186264149 1145 "To calculate the initial position, we substitute $t=0$ it into the equation $s(t)=(2t+1)^{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}_{0} & =s(0) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0+1)^{3} \\\\  & ={1}^{3} \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we cal